e:ev-m001-03a9529c1a a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "The electrical energy consumption of this capture-release process was calculated to be ~56 kJ mol−1 CO2" .

e:ev-m001-bd2ace7f9c a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "Mizen and Wrighton23 ﬁrst reported that electrogenerated 9,10-phenanthrenequinone dianion can chemically react with CO2 in homogeneous solutions to yield bis(carbonate)" .

e:ev-m001-cac75d8c22 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "a working capacity of ~6.6 mmol g−1 could still be obtained" .

e:ev-m003-aeb77fb146 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "In aprotic electrolytes, the two-electron reduction of 2-AAQ generates two nucleophilic centers (Figure 4, ﬁrst reaction), which react with electrophilic CO2 to form the corresponding biscarbonate (below)." .

e:ev-m004-ca56014ad0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "CO2 capacity (mol CO2/mol Na2Q) 1.0 0.4 0.4 0.9 0.3 0.0" .

e:ev-m004-e32a6d192d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "the CO2 capacity is 0.9 mol CO2/mol Na2Q." .

e:ev-m004-fc48c443b1 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "0.7 M Na2Q (Na2Q was prepared by QH2 and NaOH with a molar ratio of 1:2) can achieve a CO2 absorption capacity of 0.9 mol CO2/mol Na2Q." .

e:ev-m005-2db54858c2 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "Upon reduction of the neutral quinone to the radical anion, it binds a CO2 molecule" .

e:ev-m005-a9fc7be34d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "indicating the species reacts with CO2 in a chemical step." .

e:ev-m007-177dfd44a0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "This can be understood in terms of the proposed reaction of the reduced AQ species with CO2 forming [AQ-(CO2)2]2−" .

e:ev-m007-8e0f09a996 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "this sequential band appearance can be interpreted as the formation of the 1,4-NH2-AQ2−dianionic species with coordinating CO2 interaction and single-bound CO2" .

e:ev-m007-c503cfeded a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "absorption at 417 and 492 nm was observed which correlate to covalently single and dual bound [X-AQ-(CO2)n]2−species" .

e:ev-m008-0d217bc09f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "corresponding to the dianion quinone−CO2 complex formation" .

e:ev-m008-f1edf71abe a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "this analysis gives a value of 6.61 × 102 M−1 for the CO2 association constant." .

e:ev-m009-1d3ff11dcc a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "energy consumption is demonstrated as low as 113 kJ per mole of CO2 captured" .

e:ev-m009-822fdaf66b a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "We note that the gas mixture of N2 and CO2 was used here for the cell operation due to the oxygen sensitivity of quinones." .

e:ev-m009-d0128f9878 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "formation of carbonate at one of the carbonyl groups makes the quinone aromatic ring relatively neutral, leading to a facilitated reduction of second carbonyl group that leads to nucleophilic addition of another CO2 [forming quinone bis(carbonate)]" .

e:ev-m011-171e6ba4ab a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "This ΔE value corresponds to a minimum calculated work of 23.3 kJ/mol CO2 captured, or 24% energetic efficiency" .

e:ev-m011-226f480208 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "At 2M ethanol concentration, ΔE drops to 220 mV between 10 to 100% CO2, lowering the calculated work required to just 21.5 kJ/mol" .

e:ev-m011-4e260c5090 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "While these values are slightly lower than those measured using voltametric methods (log(KCO2) = 3.7 ± 0.2 and 4.3 ± 0.2  for DMF and 2M ethanol in DMF, respectively)" .

e:ev-m011-7162deaf31 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "TCQ2– reacts with CO2 to form an aryl carbonate" .

e:ev-m011-729aa1a02f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "Using this method, the log(KCO2) of TCQ2– is 3.7 ± 0.2 in the absence of hydrogen-bond donors in DMF." .

e:ev-m011-8aebdf52ae a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "The use of ethanol as an additive to TCQ-based eCCC systems provides enhanced O2 stability, which is essential for practical eCCC." .

e:ev-m011-c55f93bcfe a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "The initial and final headspace CO2 concentration and charge passed corresponds to a 95% Faradaic efficiency (FE) and 98% yield of released CO2 based on the moles of TCQ2– in solution." .

e:ev-m011-cd70c830d6 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "The CO2 concentration in the headspace decreased from 36.3% to 15% (v/v), resulting in a 73% FE for the re-capture step." .

e:ev-m012-12853fa911 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "2ClNQ, 2ClQ, and 4ClQ, the calculated free energies of binding are in close agreement with the experimental values." .

e:ev-m012-21c0d89304 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Experiments suggest that the there is no measurable binding between the DDQ2" .

e:ev-m012-88fe24a99f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "A peculiar observation about 2ClQ is that although it falls in the electron-poor category, it binds two equivalents of CO2." .

e:ev-m013-254573a040 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "The anodic peak potential of the composite under CO2 conditions is significantly positively shifted compared to that under nitrogen conditions (from −0.251 V to 0.065 V)." .

e:ev-m013-34f725ce2a a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "where the CO2 molecule carboxylates the quinone to produce carbonate" .

e:ev-m014-1473963736 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Quinones have been known to form adducts with CO2 in their reduced state via nucleophilic addition reactions for many years" .

e:ev-m014-a2dee925aa a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 12 ;
    qn:quote "even in the presence of O2, the LQ was able to capture CO2 and release all of that captured gas" .

e:ev-m015-27659f47fd a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Here Q(CO2)2−is the monocarbonate dianion." .

e:ev-m015-b2a80c8f9e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "The changes in the data support some reactivity of AQ with O2 (Figure S5)." .

e:ev-m015-e162726fdc a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "For the EEC scheme, the computed Gibbs free energy change ΔGC° increases by 20 kJ mol−1 upon the substitution of 1−8 F atoms." .

e:ev-m016-1d93274520 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "kbimolecular is 43.8 M−1 s−1 in the presence of 100 mM NaClO4" .

e:ev-m016-27e29464ac a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "the bimolecular rate constant is 162 M−1 s−1 in 100 mM NBu4ClO4" .

e:ev-m016-b4b641e347 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "drops to only 7.5 M−1 s−1 when using NaTFSI" .

e:ev-m016-c1f5d1bde9 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "reduced quinones can chemically react with CO2 via nucleophilic addition to form stable adducts" .

e:ev-m016-fc0b181986 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "drops to only 6 M−1 s−1 in 100 mM LiClO4" .

e:ev-m017-44f8607c63 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "It can be concluded that the theoretical carbon dioxide capture capacity of PAQ/MWCNTs is 9.26 mm olg-1." .

e:ev-m017-b032dba886 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "The actual carbon dioxide capture capacity of the prepared PAQ/MWCNTs composite is 7.80 mm olg-1" .

e:ev-m017-b8f2adb8af a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "it will combine with the carbon dioxide to form the PAQ-CO2 adduct." .

e:ev-m018-bd8252d76b a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "It was demonstrated that in this ionic liquid, the quinone redox behavior was similar to that of other nonaqueous systems, forming dianion adduct species with CO2 in their reduced state." .

e:ev-m019-49b5f9350a a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "a radical anion forms at the first cathodic potential (E1 = −1.15 V) and the dianion forms at the second reduction step (E2 = −1.75 V)" .

e:ev-m019-96a6cb00d0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "The half-wave potential (E1/2) of [BAQMIM][TFSA] (E1/2 = −1.15 V) shows a slightly positive shift in the redox potential compared with that of the pristine AQ" .

e:ev-m019-a293a3ad12 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "the nucleophilic oxygen atom of Q·−chemically reacts with CO2 to form a carboxylated quinone radical anion (Q(CO2)·−)." .

e:ev-m019-ba90e75efe a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "compared with that of the pristine AQ (E1/2 = −1.19 V) due to the electron-withdrawing effect of the positively charged butylimidazolium pendant." .

e:ev-m021-04bee34a3b a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 12 ;
    qn:quote "indicating that such a weak adsorption is favorable for the electro-swing system of CO2 capture/release." .

e:ev-m021-2e6fd94fad a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "only one reversible redox wave was detected at E1/2 = −1.2 V versus Ag/AgNO3 under CO2" .

e:ev-m021-3b76263a17 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "The reduction potential of BTZ under CO2 is −1.8 V versus Ag/AgNO3" .

e:ev-m021-449db3aa49 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "suggesting that the adsorption mode of reduced AQ with CO2 is physisorption." .

e:ev-m021-4cd0cdfdb0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "The reduction potential of PBTZ under N2 is detected at −2.05 V" .

e:ev-m021-a4a02e5e5f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "a reversible redox reaction of BTZ (BTZ + e−↔BTZ• −) occurs at E1/2 = −1.8 V versus Ag/AgNO3" .

e:ev-m021-b664630327 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 11 ;
    qn:quote "ΔG of BTZ−(CO2−)2 formation at ε = 10 was calculated to be −36.3 kJ/mol" .

e:ev-m021-da7f694bae a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "The ΔG values of AQ−CO2− and AQ−(CO2−)2 were calculated to be 15.1 and −7.3 kJ/mol at ε = 10, respectively." .

e:ev-m022-08d0b4f2b8 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "electrochemical reduction to form a radical anion (1 electron reduction) or dianion (2 electron reduction) activates this molecule to bind CO2 in either an EECC or ECEC (E = electron transfer, C = chemical reaction) mechanism" .

e:ev-m022-2fb40a5fcd a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "control experiments on the unfunctionalized carbon, u-CMK-3, also showed a small amount of reversible CO2 capture with an initial adsorption capacity of 0.15 mmol g−1" .

e:ev-m022-3cb83ec3b9 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "Following initial losses, the CO2 adsorption capacity began to stabilize around 0.2 mmol g−1." .

e:ev-m023-06c22641ed a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "compared to f-YP-80F (211.5 ± 24.5 kJ/molCO2)" .

e:ev-m023-29fba997ae a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "and f-BP-1300 (197.4 ± 33.3 kJ/molCO2)" .

e:ev-m023-531fa08aa0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "indicating the capture of CO2 (Fig. 6B)" .

e:ev-m023-daba3e57b9 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "f-CMK-3 had the highest energy consumption (281.6 ± 24.1 kJ/molCO2)" .

e:ev-m023-f01a63ea9a a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "The initial CO2 adsorption capacity of f-ABP (0.2 mmol/g) was lower than what was observed for f-BP-1300" .

e:ev-m024-2163597bca a qn:Evidence ;
