    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "Re(CO)5Cl(phendione)19 −0.12 −0.77 0.14 0.20 5.4" .

e:ev-m058-c15a8f1c60 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "reversible interaction between the reduced quinonoid site and CO2" .

e:ev-m058-c4361babd8 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "chitosan−rhenium −0.09 −0.69 0.32 0.36 8.3" .

e:ev-m059-d27231bad7 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "ATR-SEIRAS studies of the system show the formation of a Li2CO3 solid-electrolyte layer as well as the formation of a bis-CO2 adduct with the quinone dianion." .

e:ev-m060-1d17491b9f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "the average CO2 capture energy consumption for the AQ system reaches as high as 498.23 kJ⋅mol−1 CO2" .

e:ev-m060-31bca872fd a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "2,6-AQS (59 kJ⋅mol−1)" .

e:ev-m060-5c0c83608d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "the reduced anion radicals rapidly undergo chemical reactions with CO2" .

e:ev-m060-6e0fa171ac a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "Its average coulombic efficiency was 85.06%" .

e:ev-m060-70c171f24e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "corresponding to a log(Kbinding) as high as 16.07" .

e:ev-m060-7bb60d5692 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "low average coulombic efficiency of 56.67%" .

e:ev-m060-8d0f993fb2 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "2,7-AQS (64 kJ⋅mol−1)" .

e:ev-m060-996ef7389a a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "the average capture energy consumption for 2-AQS was only 285.92 kJ⋅mol−1 CO2" .

e:ev-m060-b34884f9bb a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "1,5-AQS (97 kJ⋅mol−1)" .

e:ev-m060-e9da39feef a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "AQ (−1.33 V vs. Fc+/Fc)" .

e:ev-m061-3860ed3d86 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "which was significantly lower than that of the original electrolyte (73.43 kJ/mol)." .

e:ev-m061-49be5acfa1 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "The first redox event occurred at a half-wave potential E1/2(Q/Q−1) of about −0.55 V vs Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m061-4ea051f267 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "This suggested that constructing intermolecular hydrogen-bonding networks is beneficial for alleviating the O2 stability problem of quinone molecules with strong CO2 complexation." .

e:ev-m061-57e63df97c a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "The second redox event appeared at a half-wave potential E1/2(Q−1/Q−2) of approximately −1.23 V vs Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m061-6aeba1120b a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "simultaneously, an appropriate Log(KCO2) (8.55) was still maintained at this time" .

e:ev-m061-6d55f404e1 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "its estimated Log(KCO2) decreased from 13.06 to 7.14." .

e:ev-m061-9738bcab71 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "the kbimolecular obtained under the test conditions was approximately 200 M−1 s−1." .

e:ev-m061-bb0cf3bae8 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 9 ;
    qn:quote "When the concentration of EG in the electrolyte was 0.036 M, its estimated Log(KCO2) decreased from 13.06 to 7.14." .

e:ev-m061-e66140cb08 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "the estimated minimum energy consumption of the electrochemical system was 50.94 kJ/mol" .

e:ev-m061-e7bc77b998 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 10 ;
    qn:quote "EG has the smallest electrochemical CO2 capture energy consumption (40.33 kJ/mol), corresponding to an EG concentration of 0.036 M." .

e:ev-m061-ee0e4f3c7e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "react with the electrophilic carbon center in the CO2 molecule to form the carboxylated quinone radical anion (PAQ(CO2)•−)" .

e:ev-m062-0287f46a81 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "The unsubstituted AQ was situated between these two groups, and its half-wave potential (≈−1.180 V) acted as a reference benchmark" .

e:ev-m062-1a2167de26 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "After introducing saturated CO2 into the solution (blue curve in Fig. 1a), a main reduction peak was observed at −0.980 V (vs. Ag/AgCl)" .

e:ev-m062-1a309d84bd a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "for instance, the E1/2 of 1-NH2-AQ decreased to −1.256 V." .

e:ev-m062-3bca10af32 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "The generation of the semiquinone radical AQ⋅- through a single-electron transfer at the first cathodic potential (E1 = −0.906 V)" .

e:ev-m062-53477a8dd6 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Specifically, the generated AQ⋅- first undergoes rapid nucleophilic addition with CO2, forming an AQ-CO2 ⋅- adduct intermediate." .

e:ev-m062-63ff2fcd1f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "followed by the formation of the quinone dianion AQ2⁻ (E2 = −1.457 V) through a second single-electron transfer" .

e:ev-m062-935d5d5ab2 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "specifically, the E1/2 of 1-Cl- AQ reached −1.155 V, representing the most positive reduction poten­ tial among all compounds depicted in the figure." .

e:ev-m063-16a879daff a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "In 0.2 M HCl (simulating Mode I), AQDS exhibits a redox potential of +0.009 V vs. Ag/AgCl." .

e:ev-m063-44cbb4fde0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "which then reacts with AQDS2−to form the AQDS(CO2)2 2−precipitate." .

e:ev-m063-4a7ef781b2 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Under 0.2 M Li2CO3 (simulating Mode II), the potential cathodically shifts to −0.467 V vs. Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m063-78870ed71d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "corresponding to a CO2 capture faradaic eﬃciency of 67%." .

e:ev-m063-7e10de6e61 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "increasing the practical energy demand to 257 kJ mol−1 CO2 for the coupled electrolyzer-hydrogen pump system." .

e:ev-m063-9dc99b269f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "The minimum theoretical energy input for CO2 capture via this AQDS-mediated process is 173 kJ mol−1 CO2" .

e:ev-m074-07f8614c30 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "For benzoateQX, the recorded values are E1 at −0.36 V" .

e:ev-m074-15c757c67e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "followed by a second cathodic potential (E2) at −1.05 V" .

e:ev-m074-274d04ca0e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "methoxyQX −0,34 −0.88 0.05 0.46 9.3" .

e:ev-m074-3127b7e959 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "phenylQX −0.33 −1.01 0.12 0.59 11.4" .

e:ev-m074-8144ce8beb a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "In the case of methoxyQX, the observed potentials are E1 at −0.38 V" .

e:ev-m074-835bfe3052 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "benzoateQX −0,29 −0.86 0.02 0.10 3.4" .

e:ev-m074-d95f1044a3 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "For phenylQX, the first cathodic potential (E1) appears at −0.36 V" .

e:ev-m077-94120f2a31 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "the binding of a second CO2 to the dianion of BQ-Cl4 is unfavorable" .

e:ev-m078-1de2797843 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 2 ;
    qn:quote "CO2(g) + OH− (aq)⇄HCO3 − (aq)" .

e:ev-m078-a3bc6156d0 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "attributable to the reoxidation of the working electrolyte through the well-known reaction with O2" .

