    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "DMSO −1.50 5.5 ± 0.9" .

e:ev-m005-acaa297e08 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "MeCN −1.51 5.3 ± 0.6" .

e:ev-m008-31a8aebe95 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "AQ-Cl and AQ-COO-C3H7 were 2.35 × 105 and 7.78 × 107 M−1, respectively." .

e:ev-m008-9a444ba98c a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "with the ﬁrst and second half-wave potentials at −1.12 and −2.15 V, respectively (Figure 1a)" .

e:ev-m008-b43cd7fb68 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "BQ-Cl4 showed two one-electron transfer processes with the ﬁrst half-wave potential at −0.39 V and the second at −1.32 V." .

e:ev-m008-b8c2c2d9d8 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "with half-wave potentials at −1.23 and −1.96 V (Figure 1b)" .

e:ev-m008-d700778ae5 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "The CO2 association constants with the BQ-Cl2 and p-NQ-Cl2 dianions are 8.18 × 105 and 7.32 × 104 M−1, respectively." .

e:ev-m011-bd4b1eaf62 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "From this data, TCQ2– has values of log(KCO2) = 2.97 ± 0.04 and 3.4 ± 0.2 in pure DMF and 2M ethanol in DMF, respectively." .

e:ev-m012-cfb7abfa1f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 5 ;
    qn:quote "4ClQ is the only quinone studied which avoids O2 reduction while still exhibiting CO2 binding as predicted by DFT and observed experimentally" .

e:ev-m015-78ff63874e a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "at potentials of E1° = −1.3 V and E2° = −1.9 V vs Fc+/Fc, respectively" .

e:ev-m015-7c697f974c a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "Figure 3a shows that the computed EEE° values increase from −1.54 to −1.17 V against Fc+/Fc upon the substitution of 1−8 F atoms" .

e:ev-m016-9190bd5c80 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "kbimolecular increases from 27.2 M−1 s−1 without additives to a plateaued value of ∼65 M−1 s−1 at n-butanol above 200 mM" .

e:ev-m018-be33b9fb28 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "In DMSO under N2, NQ-G2 exhibits two redox waves at −1.2 and −1.8 V vs Fc/Fc+, corresponding to reduction to a semiquinone radical anion species and then the dianion quinone." .

e:ev-m021-1232cac957 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "two reversible redox waves were observed at E1/2 = −1.25 and −1.7 V versus Ag/AgNO3 under N2" .

e:ev-m021-167d621d29 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "Under CO2, the waveform of PAQ shows two reduction waves (−1.2 and −1.35 V)" .

e:ev-m021-55fa6590fc a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "The CV of PAQ shows two reversible redox waves at E1/2 = −1.25 and −1.4 V versus Ag/AgNO3 under N2" .

e:ev-m022-35a0debedb a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "Adsorption capacity values of around 0.4 mmol g−1 were seen with an energy consumption of 256 kJ mol−1" .

e:ev-m035-17a006f7eb a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "Under nitrogen atmosphere, the half-wave potentials for Re(CO)3Cl(phendione) are observed at −0.12 V and −0.77 V vs Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m035-4602942015 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "and for Re(CO)3Cl(AQphen) at −0.30 V and −0.79 V vs Ag/AgCl, respectively." .

e:ev-m039-343776e870 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "yielding values of 5.8 for [Ru(bpy)2(phendione)]2+ and 7.2 for [Ru(bpy)2(NQphen)]2+" .

e:ev-m039-5d90298dba a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "suggesting the reversible formation of adducts, similar to carbonates, between the oxygen anion of the reduced quinone and the electrophilic carbon of CO2." .

e:ev-m041-e65c68b02d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "This cycle, conducted at 40 mA cm⁻² with 3 h of exposure to oxygen during capture, achieved 87% Coulombic efficiency and an 82% release-to-capture ratio at an energy cost of 157 kJ/mol CO2." .

e:ev-m044-494d215e45 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "oxidation features that grow in at increasing concentrations of CO2 are attributed to CO2 adduct reoxidation and CO2 release." .

e:ev-m045-c190c34fb5 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 4 ;
    qn:quote "Under argon, the CV displays two distinct redox peaks at −1.28 V (i) and −2.01 V (ii)" .

e:ev-m046-5649910cbe a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "However, when looking at the Faradaic efficiency, it drastically increases under extreme conditions, with 92% at pH 2 and 77% at pH 11." .

e:ev-m049-969aca06ab a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "Under the experimental conditions, the energy consumption for [EMIM][Ac] and [EMIM][PF6] was reduced to 49.69 kJ/mol and 45.54 kJ/mol, respectively." .

e:ev-m051-259364a4db a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "the E1/2 increased from −0.469 V for the amine monomer (2,7-diaminophenanthrene-9,10-dione) to +0.095 V for the COF" .

e:ev-m051-4b0241d1d6 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "compared to 43% and 53% in flue gas" .

e:ev-m051-ab1b594fbe a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "Coulombic efficiencies were similarly stable, with 46% for capture and 55% for release in N2" .

e:ev-m053-8593df67e5 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 6 ;
    qn:quote "AQDS and AQS, which achieved EU efficiencies of 87% and 66%, respectively." .

e:ev-m057-a71a66be43 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 3 ;
    qn:quote "the two well-separated reduction waves centered at approximately −1.3 V and −1.9 V vs. Fc+/Fc" .

e:ev-m058-6a900c566d a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "half-wave potentials located at approximately −0.20 V and −0.81 V vs Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m058-9a5472bd03 a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 7 ;
    qn:quote "half-wave potentials at −0.11 V and −0.69 V vs Ag/AgCl" .

e:ev-m077-e3fbbbd12f a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 8 ;
    qn:quote "it is favorable for PQ-I2 and p-NQ, which then in Figure 6c yields the mixed formation of A(CO2)2− and A(CO2)2 2−" .

e:ev-m078-ffa46d524c a qn:Evidence ;
    qn:evidenceSource qn:FullText ;
    qn:page 1 ;
    qn:quote "Energy consumption decreased from 86.1 kJ⋅mol−1 (bulk) to 66.7 kJ⋅mol−1 (in-situ)" .

